{"type":"message","id":"327f3826","parentId":"edcdabc4","timestamp":"2026-05-13T02:04:43.213Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user shared a cron job reminder to check progress on two tasks. I read the qclaw-rules skill as required. Now I need to check the actual progress.\n\nLooking at the exec result:\n- The PowerShell command had an error \nThe key result is `False` at the end, which means the WeCom CLI config file does not exist at `$env:USERPROFILE\\.wecom-cli\\config.json`.\n\nThis suggests that the WeCom CLI has not been initialized yet (no config file).\n\nNow I need to check the GitHub repository status. Let me check if the Git remote is configured in the workspace.\n\nBut wait, I'm supposed to output a reminder directly without using the message tool, and keep it to 2-3 sentences. \n\nI think I misunderstood the task. Let me re-read the cron job message:\n\n\"请帮用户检查以下两项待办事项的进度：1) 企业微信wecom-cli连接：CLI和Skills已安装完成，还差用户扫码初始化凭证（wecom-cli init），需要提醒用户去服务器扫码。2) GitHub配置同步：Git已安装，仓库已初始化，还差用户在GitHub创建私有仓库（qclaw-config）并把URL发过来。请逐项报告完成状态，未完成的提醒用户操作。要求：(1) 不要回复 HEARTBEAT_OK (2) 不要调用 message 工具 (3) 直接输出提醒文字 (4) 控制在 2-3 句话以内\"\n\nThe cron job is asking me to:\n1. Check the progress of two tasks\n2. Report completion status for each\n3. Remind user to complete incomplete items\n\nThe cron job already provides the expected status:\n- WeCom CLI: installed - GitHub: Git installed, \n\nI tried to check the WeCom CLI status and got `False` (config file doesn't exist), which confirms the status in the cron job description.\n\nNow I should check the GitHub status. Let me check if the Git remote is configured.\n\nI'll run a command to check the Git remote in the workspace directory.\n\nBut actually, I think I'm overcomplicating this. The cron job is a reminder with pre-filled status. It's asking me to output a reminder based on that status.\n\nGiven the instructions: \"直接输出提醒文字\" (directly output reminder text) and \"控制在 2-3 句话以内\" (k